<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Q4 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Q4 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch gross domestic product (GDP) is expected to show real growth of 3.0 percent in the fourth quarter of 1996 compared with the same period in 1995, according to a Reuter poll of bank economists.</p>
<p>This would be equal to the year-on-year increase in third</p>
<p>quarter GDP. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date---Period---Indicator-----Consensus---Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  27/2   Q4	 GDP Yr/Yr     3.0 pct     2.6/3.2    3.0</p>
<p> 0830  27/2   Q4	 GDP Qtr/Qtr   0.7 pct     0.3/0.9    0.6</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, MeesPierson, J.P.</p>
<p>Morgan, Rabobank. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
